## Keep the Lakeflow sync source on the VIEW; name the real triples source in build messages
================================================================================

Context: Review of the compute-once change found that pointing the Lakeflow
synced table at `…_data` is unsafe today. The scheduled build
(`src/back/objects/registry/schedule/build.py`) never materializes `…_data` and
registers the VIEW, and `SyncedTableManager.ensure` reuses an existing
registration by name without comparing its source. A synced table registered on
`…_data` by the main build would therefore be refreshed from a stale `…_data`
by every scheduled build. The table-source switch is deferred to a later task
that also fixes the scheduled path. The build messages still said "VIEW" while
a materialized build reads `…_data`, and two callers went through the compat
alias instead of the real count method.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/_build_pipeline.py
   `_apply_via_synced_pipeline` passes `source_table_full_name=self.view_table`
   again (and logs it), with a one-line comment at the hook. The count and the
   full-rebuild stream keep reading `_triples_source_relation()`. `with_object_hash`
   on the `…_data` CTAS is unchanged (needed when the sync source moves).
2. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/_build_pipeline.py
   `_apply_full_rebuild` names the actual source relation in the progress
   message ("Reading all triples from <relation>..."), in the "reports N triples
   to ingest" log and in the zero-triples warning. `_apply_full_rebuild` and
   `_report_post_sync_triple_count` call `_count_source_triples()` directly;
   `_count_view_triples` stays only as the compat alias. Net line count of the
   size-frozen methods is unchanged.
3. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinBuildPostMaterialize.py
   Docstring no longer claims the Lakeflow sync reads the relation.
4. tests/units/objects/test_build_pipeline_compute_once.py
   The Lakeflow source is the VIEW in both table and view mode; messages name
   the real relation (table and view mode, and the empty-source warning); the
   full rebuild and the post-sync count use `_count_source_triples`, not the alias.
5. tests/units/dtwin/test_build_pipeline_streaming.py
   Count mocks target `_count_source_triples`.

