## Per-domain `materialization_mode` setting and the readiness fallback ladder
================================================================================

Context: Task 1 of incremental triple materialization. A domain now carries a
requested materialization mode (`full`, `incremental`, `microbatch`,
`realtime`) that is persisted and editable under Domain -> General, and a
resolver turns the request into the mode that actually runs, recording why they
differ. No serverless or row-tracking probe exists yet, so the build calls the
resolver with both readiness inputs `False`: every non-`full` request resolves
to `full` and the build-run trace says why. Later tasks feed real probe inputs.
`realtime` validates but always resolves to `microbatch` first
(`realtime_not_available`) in this release.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/GraphDBFactory.py
   `MATERIALIZATION_MODES`, `DEFAULT_MATERIALIZATION_MODE` ("full"),
   `normalize_materialization_mode` (invalid / None / non-str -> "full") next to
   `normalize_lakehouse_materialization`, and
   `GraphDBFactory.resolve_materialization_mode(domain, settings)` returning the
   requested mode, normalized and not gated by backend.
2. src/back/core/graphdb/ModeDecision.py (new)
   Frozen dataclass `ModeDecision(requested, effective, reason)`; `reason` is ""
   when `effective == requested`. Its own file: the architecture guard allows one
   public class per file.
3. src/back/core/graphdb/MaterializationModeResolver.py (new)
   `MaterializationModeResolver.resolve(...)` applies the ladder one step at a
   time: realtime -> microbatch (`realtime_not_available`, the
   `realtime_topic_available` kwarg is accepted and ignored); incremental /
   microbatch -> full when serverless is unavailable (`serverless_unavailable`)
   or the backend is not databricks / lakebase / neo4j (`backend_not_eligible`);
   microbatch -> incremental and incremental -> full without row tracking
   (`row_tracking_missing`). The final reason is the first downgrade's.
   `previews` is accepted for a stable signature and not consulted yet.
4. src/back/core/graphdb/__init__.py
   Re-export `MaterializationModeResolver` and `ModeDecision`.
5. src/back/objects/domain/Domain.py
   `materialization_mode` is read, saved and returned like
   `lakehouse_materialization` (`get_domain_info`, `save_domain_info`, its
   response and `get_domain_template_data`), coerced by
   `_coerce_materialization_mode`; an absent key keeps the stored value and an
   unknown value falls back to "full". The five graph keys that three response
   dicts repeated move into `_graph_info()` (Extract Method), which keeps
   `Domain` and `save_domain_info` under their frozen size budgets.
6. src/back/objects/session/DomainSession.py
   `materialization_mode` ("full") in the new-domain defaults, `export_for_save`
   and `import_from_file`, so the choice survives save and reload (a legacy
   export without it imports as "full"). Both methods read the info dict through
   a local alias, which keeps them and `DomainSession` under their frozen budgets.
7. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinBuildPostMaterialize.py
   `decide_mode(pipe)` calls the resolver with `serverless_available=False`,
   `sources_row_tracked=False`, `previews={}` and the domain's real graph backend
   (`_resolve_graph_backend`, which can say `none` / `neo4j`, unlike the
   triple-store backend), and logs a fallback. `trace_fields` adds
   `materialization_mode_requested`, `materialization_mode_effective` and
   `mode_fallback_reason` (full / full / "" when no decision exists).
8. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/_build_pipeline.py
   One-line hooks: `mode_decision` attribute and
   `self.mode_decision = TwinBuildPostMaterialize.decide_mode(self)` as the first
   line of `run()`'s `try`, so a build that fails during translation still
   traces its mode (`_BuildPipeline` 1410 -> 1413 LOC, baseline 1452 unchanged).
   The three trace keys are not `build_runs` columns, so they live in the
   in-memory entry only and are dropped when the row is persisted.
9. src/front/templates/partials/domain/_domain_information.html
   `#domainMaterializationMode` select (Full rebuild / Incremental / Micro-batch /
   Real-time, disabled "later release") in its own `#materializationModeSection`
