## SlotProjectionCompiler: row-local mappings to Lakeflow slot-event SQL
================================================================================

Context: Task 2 of incremental triple materialization. The incremental modes keep
a `_slots` streaming table (key = `(map_id, source_key, predicate)`) in sync with
the source tables' change feed. Mappings that read one table with plain column
predicates ("row-local") can be projected per source row; joins, `sql_query`
sources and reference predicates stay on the batch path. This adds the compiler
for the row-local side as a new `back/core/streaming/` subpackage; nothing calls
it yet (the pipeline runner and the build dispatch are later tasks).

Changes:

1. src/back/core/streaming/SlotProjectionCompiler.py (new)
   Static-method compiler. `classify` returns `row_local` / `batch` (table without
   `sql_query`, a column in the subject template, only `column` predicates, safe
   identifiers; a table-based relationship with plain subject and object columns).
   `map_id` = `map_` + SHA-1 of the canonical mapping JSON (source, subject
   template, class, label column, predicates) truncated to 12 hex chars.
   `source_key_expr` gives `CAST(pk AS STRING)` or `concat_ws('|', ...)` for a
   composite template. `slot_event_view_sql` emits the temporary view over
   `STREAM <table> WITH (readChangeFeed = true)` with a `LATERAL VIEW stack(...)`
   whose pairs come from `SparqlTranslator._generic_triples_stack_predicates_for_mapping`
   and whose subject comes from `_subject_expr_from_template`; `update_preimage`
   and NULL objects become `DELETE`. `auto_cdc_flow_sql` emits the AUTO CDC flow
   in the binding clause order (KEYS, APPLY AS DELETE WHEN, SEQUENCE BY
   STRUCT(_commit_version, seq_rank), COLUMNS * EXCEPT, STORED AS SCD TYPE 1).
   `slots_table_sql` emits the clustered streaming table. `compile` walks the
   `{class_uri: mapping}` dict (a shared TriplesMap dict is compiled once per
   class as `{**mapping, "class_uri": class_uri}`, so each class has its own
   `map_id`, `slot_events_<map_id>` view and `slot_flow_<map_id>` flow) plus the
   relationship list. FQNs pass `validate_table_name` and `SAFE_SQL_IDENT`,
   columns `SAFE_COL_IDENT` (`ValidationError` otherwise; `classify` falls back to
   `batch`); class URIs, predicates and template prefixes go through `sql_escape`.
   `base_uri` is accepted and unused (templates carry their own prefix).
2. src/back/core/streaming/SlotPipelineSpec.py (new)
   Dataclass: `slots_fqn`, ordered `statements`, `row_local_map_ids`,
   `batch_mappings` (entity copies carry their `class_uri`), sorted unique
   `source_tables`, and `to_sql()` joining the statements with `;\n\n`.
3. src/back/core/streaming/__init__.py (new)
   Re-exports `SlotProjectionCompiler` and `SlotPipelineSpec` with `__all__`.
4. tests/units/streaming/__init__.py, tests/units/streaming/test_slot_projection_compiler.py (new)
   62 cases: classification (row-local, join, `sql_query`, no table, unsafe
   identifiers, relationship with and without table, extractor-shaped
   relationship is batch), `map_id` golden value / key-order independence /
   change on added predicate, source key (single, composite), view SQL content
   and escaping, AUTO CDC exact text and clause order, slots table SQL,
   `compile` partitioning, shared-dict classes getting distinct ids, views and
   flows, determinism and `to_sql()` round trip.
5. docs/architecture.md
   New "Incremental slot projection" subsection before "Reasoning Engine".

