## Fix: incremental build review round 1 (microbatch bootstrap, fingerprints, leaked pipelines, MV reuse)
================================================================================

Context: Review fix round 1 of Task 4 (five Important findings).

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinIncrementalBuild.py (Imp#1, Imp#2)
   A full refresh of the slot pipeline (new pipeline or changed SQL
   fingerprint) always runs as a TRIGGERED update to COMPLETED, so `_data` is
   never built over an empty `_slots`; a microbatch domain is then switched to
   continuous and waited for until RUNNING. While the refresh is pending the
   pipeline keeps its previous `ontobricks.slot_sql_sha256` (or ""); the new
   one is stamped (an `ensure` with the new fingerprint) only after the update
   completed, so a failed refresh is retried as a full refresh by the next
   build. Without a full refresh the previous path is unchanged.
2. src/back/core/streaming/SlotPipelineRunner.py (Imp#2)
   `ensure(..., fingerprint=None)` stores an explicit fingerprint (default: the
   SQL hash).
3. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/materialize.py (Imp#3)
   `apply_data_relation` drops a leftover `_data` MATERIALIZED VIEW (best-effort)
   in both branches before the existing cross-drops, so `/dtwin/databricks-build`
   and every full build can replace it. TwinIncrementalBuild now only drops a
   `_graph` MV itself. New best-effort `relation_exists` (SHOW TABLES).
4. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinIncrementalBuild.py (Imp#4)
   The gate exit (decision resolves to full), the fallback, and a requested
   `full` build whose `_slots` table exists stop this version's slot pipeline
   when it is active (looked up by name; failures logged and swallowed).
   Domains that never ran incrementally make no pipelines API call.
5. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/MaterializedViewBuilder.py,
   src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/TwinIncrementalBuild.py (Imp#5)
   The data MV records `'ontobricks.mv_sql_sha256'` (sha256 of the refresh
   policy and the AS SELECT body) in its TBLPROPERTIES; `data_mv_sha` and
   `existing_mv_sha` ("" on any error). An unchanged definition skips
   `CREATE OR REPLACE` and only runs `REFRESH MATERIALIZED VIEW`; the trace's
   `refresh_technique` is read after that REFRESH.
6. Tests: tests/units/objects/test_build_pipeline_modes.py (stateful fake
   runner; bootstrap, fingerprint stamping and retry, the three stop sites,
   stop failure, MV reuse both paths), tests/units/graphdb/delta/
   test_delta_package.py (MV drop in both branches, relation_exists),
   tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_materialized_view_builder.py (sha property,
   data_mv_sha, existing_mv_sha), tests/units/streaming/test_slot_pipeline_runner.py
   (explicit fingerprint).

Known limitations:
- On the Delta backend, microbatch gives no `_data` freshness between builds:
  the `_data` MV has no SCHEDULE/TRIGGER, so it only refreshes when a build runs.
- Slot pipelines of earlier versions keep running after a version bump; only the
  current version's pipeline is stopped (TODO(task-8)).
- `augment_mappings_from_config` adds `sql_query` to every configured entity, so
  most mappings classify as batch and the slot pipeline only runs for legacy
  table-based mappings; incremental is then the `_data` MV over the batch branch.

