   `TBLPROPERTIES (delta.enableRowTracking = true, delta.enableDeletionVectors
   = true)`: row tracking gives a triggered/continuous synced table its
   automatic change data feed.
9. src/back/objects/registry/schedule/build.py
   The scheduled mirror materializes `_data` (`apply_data_relation(...,
   mode="table", with_object_hash=True)`) before `mgr.ensure`, takes source,
   key and schedule from `TwinLakebaseSync.sync_plan_for` (full mode, no
   slots), drops the union view on drift and rebuilds it for the plan's
   source kind. Without a domain the gateway VIEW stays the source.
10. src/front/templates/settings.html, src/front/static/config/js/settings.js
    The Lakeflow schedule select offers Snapshot / Triggered / Continuous with
    help text on the cap; the JS saves and restores the selected value instead
    of forcing `snapshot`.
11. docs/backend.md
    `sync_table_mode` rows describe the cap instead of "snapshot only".
